nd fix it so the program runs cleanly. When it\nworks, `python3 main.py` should print exactly:\n\n```\nTotal: 5.0\n```\n\nDone when `python3 main.py` exits successfully and prints that line.\n"], "completed": true, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 4, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "ended_et": "2026-10-26T01:20:49.715434-04:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": null, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 2, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610260331 (/h1/opencode-src/bin/b3fcc9a81dd39dc8b595b003d722b89c158cdfbc/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "thesis-h1-cpu.c.nyu-rdg-fy26-js11531-a68d.internal", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "machine": "thesis-h1-cpu", "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: task]\nThe first call didn't return an id, and the task tool has no parameter for passing one. I'll make the follow-up call anyway, but it may not continue the same subagent.\n[tool: task]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the crash, and `python3 main.py` now prints `Total: 5.0`.\n\n- **Cause:** `settings.json` had the key misspelled as `\"rat\"`. `get_rate()` in `app/pricing.py:8` calls `SETTINGS.get(\"rate\")`, which returned `None`. That `None` then hit `rate * count` at `app/report.py:9`.\n- **Fix:** I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"rate\"` in `settings.json`.\n- **Subagent id:** The first task call didn't return an id, and the tool has no parameter for passing one. The second call therefore went to a fresh subagent instead of continuing the first. Its answer matched the first one.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests":